    "Historical text-only promotion evidence: The five wrappers func_ov007_020cca68..020ccab4 are `bx ip` sibcall veneers under -interworking: Deallocate/LoadFile through #pragma long_calls' pooled branch, and Heap::Allocate/_Deallocate/MaxAllocationUnitSize member calls on the game heap at data_020a0ea0. func_ov007_020cca68's Deallocate signature is decl_common.h's `void Deallocate(void*)`, so the veneer takes and forwards `void *p` -- the arg lands in r0 either way and the tail branch is identical.",
    "Historical text-only promotion evidence: Declaration reconciliations recorded on the previous revision still stand: data_0209b340 stays decl_common.h's `int[]` with byte-view casts in func_ov007_020cc168; data_0209caa0 stays `int[]` (the dispatcher's trailing `data_0209caa0[0x328]` byte read is spelt ((u8*)data_0209caa0)[0x328]); data_0209b33c is `FileSaveData *` (the dispatcher needs flags1, so the opaque `struct E` gave way to the recovered 0x44 layout already used by the pre-fold file); func_ov007_020b7090 takes (u16,u16,u16,u16,int).",
    "Historical text-only promotion evidence: overlay_100/overlay_102 remain two of the pre-existing `dsd check symbols` errors (absolute ARM9-main rows at 0x64/0x66 outside every module's sections) -- baseline errors, unchanged by this fold. The TU does not reference them: its overlay operands are the lcf-defined OVERLAY_100_ID / OVERLAY_102_ID linker constants, declared `extern int` locally exactly as src/game/stages/d_s_mb.cpp does.",
    "Current data ownership uses compiler-native RTTI, names and vtables plus a typed BaseSpawnInfo<dScDSMT_c> and int pending-music definition. The profile has priorities1 and3; factory remains manual construction with a typed return. Existing public numeric vtable aliases are zero-extra-storage identities. Native bindings are retained; no symbol-binding rewrite or integer vtable is introduced.",
